BCC_Q({"lv": "910", "y": 2025, "n": 13, "part": "C", "topic": "opt", "title": "Third Game", "answer": 1, "story": "<p>Beavers Anna and Bento are playing a two-player game called Third. The game is played on a \\(3\\times3\\) board using a total of eight pieces. Each piece has three defining attributes: shape (square or circle), colour (grey or white), and marking (diamond or plain). The eight pieces are shown.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"White square, white square with a diamond, grey square, grey square with a diamond, white circle, white circle with a diamond, grey circle, grey circle with a diamond.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:4.94444in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>The game begins with an empty board. The two players take turns placing pieces on the board, however, each piece is selected by their opponent (from the pieces not currently on the board). The player then places this piece on any available square on the board. The winner is the first player to place the third piece in a row or a column so that all three pieces have the same colour, shape, or marking.<\/p>\n<p>For example, suppose the game board is as shown, and Bento chooses the <img alt=\"white circle\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.37778in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/> piece for Anna. If she places this piece in the bottom-left corner, then she will win the game because she will have placed the third piece in a column with all circles.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"A game board with three pieces placed: the white circle with a diamond is in the top-left square, the grey circle is in the leftmost square in the middle row, and the grey square is in the rightmost square in the middle row. Then, the circle piece is added to the bottom-left square and the first column of the grid is highlighted.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:5.33333in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>", "question": "<p>Bento and Anna are playing Third and after each player has placed two pieces, the board is as shown.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"A game board with four pieces placed: the grey circle is in the top-left square, the white circle is in the top-right square, the grey square is in the leftmost square in the middle row, and the white circle with a diamond is in the middle square in the bottom row.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.07222in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>It is now Bento's turn. How many of the following four pieces could Anna select for Bento if she wants to ensure that Bento <strong>cannot<\/strong> win the game on his turn?<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"white square with a diamond\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.50778in\"/> <img alt=\"white square\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.50778in\"/> <img alt=\"grey circle with a diamond\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.50778in\"/> <img alt=\"grey square with a diamond\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.50778in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<ol class=\"mc\">\n<li>0<\/li>\n<li>1<\/li>\n<li>2<\/li>\n<li>3<\/li>\n<\/ol>", "answerHtml": "<p>(B) 1<\/p>", "explanation": "<p>Bento can only complete the top row or the leftmost column on this\nturn.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>If Anna selects the <img alt=\"white square with a diamond\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.37778in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/>, then completing either the top row or the leftmost column will not result in a win for Bento.<\/p><\/li>\n<li><p>If Anna selects the <img alt=\"white square\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.37778in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/>, then Bento can win the game by completing either the top row or the\nleftmost column (three plain pieces in each case), as shown.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"The top row has grey circle, white square, and white circle.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.07222in\"/>     <img alt=\"The leftmost column has grey circle, grey square, and white square.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.07222in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<li><p>If Anna selects the <img alt=\"grey circle with a diamond\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.37778in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/>, then Bento can win the game by completing either the top row (three\ncircle pieces) or the leftmost column (three grey pieces) as shown.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"The top row has grey circle, grey circle with a diamond, and white circle.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.07222in\"/>     <img alt=\"The leftmost column has grey circle, grey square, and grey circle with a diamond.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.07222in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<li><p>If Anna selects the <img alt=\"grey square with a diamond\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.37778in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/>, then Bento can win the game by completing the leftmost column\n(three grey pieces) as shown.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"The leftmost column has grey circle, grey square, and grey square with a diamond.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.07222in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Therefore, there is only 1 piece Anna can select to ensure Bento\ncannot win the game on his turn.<\/p>", "connections": ""});